<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stockholm</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stockholm is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, built on islands where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-malaren">Lake Mälaren</a> meets the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-sea">Baltic Sea</a>. First recorded in 1252 and associated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birger-jarl">Birger Jarl</a>, it grew as a trading port with strong German and Hanseatic links and became the seat of royal government. It was the scene of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm-bloodbath">Stockholm Bloodbath</a> of 1520 and the centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> in the 17th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stockholm.jpg" alt="Stockholm" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Steven Lek · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_Dramatic_Theatre_Stockholm.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
